{"text": "8 Jul, 95 PKU WASTRESABS.D0C P 0500/5288\n\nStress induction in Rabbits by Cigarette Sidestream Smoke\n\n(Draft results from a pilot study\")\n\n4 rabbits were exposed for 6 hours to the fresh sidestream smoke (FSS) of the standard\nreference cigarette 1R4F and of a non-tobacco cigarette (X6D6MW). FSS concentrations were\n7 and 20 ug total particulate matter per liter corresponding to 20 and 60 ppm carbon\n\u2018monoxide. In addition, non-chemical stressors such as immobilization were used. The\nindividual rabbits were sequentially exposed to the different stressors with non-exposure days\ninterspersed. Effects were evaluated by comparing data obtained on exposure days to those\n\u2018on non-exposure days.\n\nThe heart rate was consistently decreased by approximately 30 % as a response to both types\nof FSS. By immobilization, the heart rate increased by approximately 15 %.\n\nCorticosterone levels in urine\u201d rose up to 2-fold following exposure to both types of FSS and\napproximately 3-fold by immobilization. Urinary cortisol did not respond.\n\nNoradrenaline levels in urine rose up to 3-fold following exposure to both types of FSS and\napproximately 2-fold by immobilization. The level of normetanephrin, @ noradrenaline\n\u2018metabolite, rose up to about 30-fold following exposure to FSS of 1R4F. But this effect was\nRot reproducible. No effect was seen on adrenalin and metanephrin levels. None of these\n\u2018compounds responded to immobilization.\n\n\u2018The other stressors used did not cause relevant stress responses.\n\nIn conclusion, the few data available do show a distinct stress response of the rabbits to FSS\n\u2018exposure, although the responses were small and show a large interindividual variation. No\ndose/response characteristics could be proven under these conditions. The FSS generated\nfrom the non-tobacco cigarette also induced stress responses, although to date, the data do\not allow a quantitative comparison to the effects seen following 1R4F FSS exposure.\n\nBased on the low number of rabbits in this study and the fact that this was the first stress study in our\nlaboratory, the results have to be considered as preliminary, Statistical evaluations have not been made\nto date,\n\nexcretion data are normalized to urinary creatinine\n\nSpzLO6Losz",
